# ProximaDB Architecture Diagrams

## System Architecture
```mermaid
graph TB
    Client[Client Applications]
    
    subgraph "API Layer"
        REST[REST API :5678]
        GRPC[gRPC API :5679]
    end
    
    subgraph "Service Layer"
        UnifiedHandlers[Unified Handlers]
        VectorOperationsService[VectorOperationsService]
        CollectionService[CollectionService]
    end
    
    subgraph "Compute Layer"
        UnifiedDistanceCompute[UnifiedDistanceCompute]
        UnifiedQuantizationEngine[UnifiedQuantizationEngine]
        HardwareAcceleration[Hardware Acceleration (SIMD/GPU)]
    end
    
    subgraph "Storage Layer"
        StorageEngine[StorageEngine]
        MemTable[MemTable]
        SST[SST Engine]
        VIPER[VIPER Engine]
        WAL[Write-Ahead Log]
        MetadataStore[Metadata Store]
    end
    
    Client --> REST & GRPC
    REST & GRPC --> UnifiedHandlers
    UnifiedHandlers --> VectorOperationsService
    UnifiedHandlers --> CollectionService
    VectorOperationsService --> StorageEngine
    VectorOperationsService --> UnifiedDistanceCompute
    VectorOperationsService --> UnifiedQuantizationEngine
    CollectionService --> MetadataStore
    StorageEngine --> MemTable
    StorageEngine --> SST
    StorageEngine --> VIPER
    StorageEngine --> WAL
    UnifiedDistanceCompute --> HardwareAcceleration
    UnifiedQuantizationEngine --> HardwareAcceleration
```

## Write Path Flow
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API Layer
    participant S as Service Layer
    participant M as MemTable
    participant W as WAL
    participant E as Storage Engine
    
    C->>A: Insert Vector Request
    A->>S: Validate & Route
    S->>W: Write to WAL
    W-->>S: ACK
    S->>M: Insert to MemTable
    M-->>S: Success
    S-->>A: Response
    A-->>C: 200 OK
    
    Note over M,E: Background Flush
    M->>E: Flush when threshold reached
    E->>E: Compress & Index
```

## Search Path Flow
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API Layer
    participant Q as Query Optimizer
    participant I as Index (AXIS)
    participant S as Storage Engine
    participant R as Result Merger
    
    C->>A: Search Request
    A->>Q: Parse & Optimize
    Q->>Q: Select Strategy
    
    alt Index Available
        Q->>I: Query Index
        I->>I: Find Candidates
        I->>S: Fetch Vectors
    else No Index
        Q->>S: Scan Storage
    end
    
    S->>R: Return Results
    R->>R: Merge & Rank
    R->>A: Top-K Results
    A->>C: Response
```

## Storage Engine Selection
```mermaid
graph LR
    W[Workload] --> D{Decision}
    
    D -->|OLTP| SST[SST Engine<br/>Row-based<br/>Fast writes]
    D -->|OLAP| VIPER[VIPER Engine<br/>Columnar<br/>Compression]
    D -->|Mixed| NOVA[NOVA Engine<br/>Hybrid<br/>Adaptive]
    D -->|Stream| SWIFT[SWIFT Engine<br/>Hierarchical<br/>High throughput]
    D -->|Edge| PRISM[PRISM Engine<br/>LSM-tree<br/>Low memory]
```

## Hardware Acceleration
```mermaid
graph TB
    Q[Query] --> H{Hardware Detection}
    
    H -->|CPU| SIMD{SIMD Available?}
    SIMD -->|AVX-512| AVX512[AVX-512 Kernel]
    SIMD -->|AVX2| AVX2[AVX2 Kernel]
    SIMD -->|NEON| NEON[ARM NEON Kernel]
    SIMD -->|No| SCALAR[Scalar Fallback]
    
    H -->|GPU| GPU{GPU Type}
    GPU -->|NVIDIA| CUDA[CUDA Kernel]
    GPU -->|AMD| ROCM[ROCm Kernel]
    GPU -->|Apple| MPS[Metal Kernel]
```

## Data Tiering
```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Hot Tier"
        HOT[In-Memory<br/>< 1 hour old]
    end
    
    subgraph "Warm Tier"
        WARM[SSD Storage<br/>1 hour - 1 day]
    end
    
    subgraph "Cold Tier"
        COLD[Object Storage<br/>> 1 day old]
    end
    
    HOT -->|Age| WARM
    WARM -->|Age| COLD
    COLD -.->|Access| WARM
    WARM -.->|Access| HOT
```

## Deployment Options
```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Single Server"
        S1[ProximaDB<br/>All-in-one]
    end
    
    subgraph "High Availability"
        LB[Load Balancer]
        S2[ProximaDB Primary]
        S3[ProximaDB Standby]
        SHARED[Shared Storage<br/>S3/NFS]
        
        LB --> S2
        LB -.-> S3
        S2 --> SHARED
        S3 --> SHARED
    end
    
    subgraph "Distributed"
        R[Router]
        SH1[Shard 1<br/>Collections A-M]
        SH2[Shard 2<br/>Collections N-Z]
        
        R --> SH1
        R --> SH2
    end
```
